  "literature_notes": "All eight ledger lines were evaluated. L1 (PMC12356840) is the only clip that states a tag position: an N-terminal FLAG+Strep tag on full-length SLC26A7. The topology landmarks place residues 1\u201350 in the INTRACELLULAR compartment, so this tag faces the cytoplasm, not the extracellular space \u2014 it qualifies only as an intracellular tag and is recorded in other_positions. L2\u2013L5 and L8 (PMC6656751, PMC6237461) report FLAG-tagged SLC26A7 constructs whose surface display is confirmed by immunofluorescence in MDCK cells or in transgenic mice, but none of these clips states the residue or junction at which the FLAG tag was inserted. The 'position unstated' disqualification rule applies: we cannot pin insert_after_residue. The topology_derived escape hatch (exactly one extracellular terminus) cannot rescue these clips either, because SLC26A7 has zero extracellular termini \u2014 both the N-terminus (residues 1\u201350, INTRACELLULAR) and the C-terminus (residues 474\u2013656, INTRACELLULAR) face the cytoplasm. The FLAG tag in those constructs must reside in one of the six extracellular loops (EC 72\u201377, 116\u2013146, 196\u2013227, 279\u2013308, 402\u2013403, 452\u2013454), but which loop is not stated anywhere in the ledger. L6\u2013L7 (PMC6237461) report GFP-tagged SLC26A7 at the plasma membrane with no position stated; GFP at either terminus would be intracellular, and no loop is named. No ledger line therefore supports a pinnable extracellular surface tag site.",
